Test SEP-2663 dispatch / envelope rules across the tasks surface.

[1mServer Implementation Requirements:[0m

[1mRemoved v1 methods (SEP-2663):[0m
- [2mtasks/result[0m is removed in v2 — the result is inlined on
  [2mtasks/get[0m. Servers MUST reject the method with JSON-RPC [2m-32601[0m.
- [2mtasks/list[0m is removed in v2. Servers MUST reject it with
  [2m-32601[0m.

[1mServer-directed task creation (SEP-2663):[0m
- The client does NOT send a [2mtask[0m hint param. The server alone
  decides whether to create a task. A [2mtools/call[0m against a
  task-supporting tool MUST produce [2mCreateTaskResult[0m even with no
  client hint.

[1mLegacy [2mtask[0m param tolerated (SEP-2663):[0m
- A v1 client may still send [2mtask: { ttl, pollInterval }[0m on
  [2mtools/call[0m. The server MUST tolerate it (no error) AND MUST NOT
  promote a sync-only tool to a task on its presence. The body
  arguments + tool registration are authoritative.

[1mImmediate-result shortcut (SEP-2663):[0m
- A server MAY return a sync [2mToolResult[0m for task-supporting tools
  when the operation completes fast enough. Either return a
  [2mCreateTaskResult[0m (with [2mresultType:"task"[0m) or a sync
  [2mToolResult[0m (with [2mresultType:"complete"[0m); both are valid.

[1mresultType:"complete" on non-task responses (SEP-2322):[0m
- Every JSON-RPC response on the tools+tasks surface other than a
  CreateTaskResult MUST carry [2mresultType:"complete"[0m. This applies
  to: sync [2mtools/call[0m, [2mtasks/get[0m, [2mtasks/update[0m ack,
  [2mtasks/cancel[0m ack.

[1mStrong consistency / durable create (SEP-2663):[0m
- A server MUST NOT return [2mCreateTaskResult[0m until the task is
  durably created — that is, until a [2mtasks/get[0m for the returned
  [2mtaskId[0m would resolve. Issuing [2mtasks/get[0m immediately after the
  CreateTaskResult arrives MUST succeed, not -32602.

[1mUnknown taskId on tasks/get (SEP-2663):[0m
- [2mtasks/get[0m for a taskId the server doesn't recognize MUST return
  JSON-RPC [2m-32602[0m (InvalidParams). Mirrors the same rule for
  [2mtasks/cancel[0m (clarified upstream in spec commit d963ad0).

[1mRequired server fixtures ([2mtools/list[0m MUST include all):[0m
- [2mgreet[0m — sync-only.
- [2mslow_compute[0m — task-supporting ([2mseconds: 0[0m for the immediate
  shortcut path).
- [2mconfirm_delete[0m — task-supporting, parks for elicitation.
- [2mfailing_job[0m — task-supporting, returns a tool execution error.
